 ],
 "literal": "Because it exists indeed, behold, this world, if the gods' / nectar of immortality is obtained, even if it is sweet, saying, / alone, eating, they do not indeed; they have no anger; / slumbering, they do not; what others fear, fearing; / if it is fame, even life they will give; if it is blame, / even if they receive the world together with it, they will not accept; they have no weariness; / such greatness, those who are like that, having become, / for themselves, saying, not striving, with strong effort, / for others, saying, those who strive, because of their existence indeed.",
 "translation": "Behold, this world exists because of those who, even if they were to obtain the nectar of the gods, would not eat it alone, thinking it sweet; they bear no malice; they do not slumber in laziness, but fear what others fear; they would give up their very lives for fame, but would not accept blame even if they were to gain the whole world; they are free from weariness; having attained such greatness, they do not strive for themselves, but with strong effort, they strive for others.",
 "modern": "இந்த உலகம் நிலைபெற்றிருப்பதற்குக் காரணம், தேவர்களின் அமிழ்தமே கிடைப்பதாயினும் அது இனிமையானது என்று தனித்து உண்ணாதவர்கள்; யாரிடமும் வெறுப்புக் கொள்ளாதவர்கள்; சோம்பலின்றிச் செயல்படுபவர்கள்; பிறர் அஞ்சுவதற்குத் தாமும் அஞ்சுபவர்கள்; புகழ் கிடைக்குமென்றால் தம் உயிரையும் கொடுப்பவர்கள்; பழி வரும் என்றால் இந்த உலகம் முழுவதையும் பெற்றாலும் ஏற்றுக்கொள்ளாதவர்கள்; சோர்வில்லாதவர்கள்; இத்தகைய பெருமைகளை உடையவர்களாகி, தமக்காக உழைக்காமல், பிறருக்காகத் தம் வலிமையான முயற்சியால் உழைப்பவர்கள் இருப்பதனால்தான்.",
 "explanation": "This poem is spoken by the poet Kadalul Mayndha Ilamperu Vazhudhi under the theme of Porunmozhi Kanchi (counseling on the path of virtue) in the Potuviyal tinai. The poet explains why the world continues to exist despite all its troubles: it is because of the presence of noble, selfless human beings. These noble people do not enjoy even the nectar of immortality alone, they bear no hatred, they do not succumb to laziness, and they fear what is truly fearful. They value honor above life itself and reject infamy even if offered the entire world. By striving tirelessly not for themselves but for the welfare of others, they sustain the world.",
 "model": "gemini-3.5-flash",
 "generated": "2026-11-26"
}